   "file": "content/FMA_21376/tier1.md",
   "text": "Each great saphenous vein drains blood from the superficial, or near-surface, parts of the inner leg and thigh. This long vein begins at veins on the big toe and foot, then runs up the inner leg. Each great saphenous vein empties into the femoral vein, which drains the upper leg.",
